Ben, I have a sad story to tell you.

01:58:09.500 --> 01:58:09.840
Oh, really?

01:58:09.940 --> 01:58:12.660
Many years ago, a couple had twin sons.

01:58:13.000 --> 01:58:14.380
One named Juan.

01:58:14.820 --> 01:58:15.140
Juan?

01:58:15.260 --> 01:58:16.860
And one named Amal.

01:58:17.220 --> 01:58:17.660
Amal.

01:58:17.990 --> 01:58:21.750
And the twins grew to adulthood and left home to seek their fortune.

01:58:21.990 --> 01:58:22.130
Okay.

01:58:22.330 --> 01:58:24.890
Juan stayed in the small town his parents lived in,

01:58:25.050 --> 01:58:27.660
but Amal moved away to Europe.

01:58:27.880 --> 01:58:28.320
Do tell.

01:58:28.560 --> 01:58:29.980
And his mother complained to her husband...

01:58:30.000 --> 01:58:36.440
husband, oh, I miss Amal so. I'm glad Juan is here so I can see him all the time, but

01:58:36.660 --> 01:58:44.740
I want to see Amal. And her husband said, dear, they're identical twins. They look exactly

01:58:44.740 --> 01:58:52.970
alike. And you know the old saying, you've seen Juan, you've seen Amal. Our thanks to

01:58:52.970 --> 01:58:57.840
Jack Taylor for that joke. You didn't actually enjoy that, did you? No, but it's the way

01:58:57.840 --> 01:58:59.740
Thank you

01:59:00.570 --> 01:59:01.650
Our thanks to Jack Taylor.

01:59:02.390 --> 01:59:04.130
And the Jack Taylor Dancers.

01:59:07.520 --> 01:59:08.550
Good night, everybody.

01:59:09.090 --> 01:59:10.010
You've seen one.

01:59:13.450 --> 01:59:17.130
I think we've all learned a big lesson from that one, right?

01:59:19.340 --> 01:59:20.580
Jack Taylor, the writing credit.

01:59:20.760 --> 01:59:21.700
Thank you very much.

01:59:21.800 --> 01:59:23.460
We're glad you tuned in this week.

01:59:23.800 --> 01:59:26.440
And we hope you'll tune in again next week.

01:59:27.100 --> 01:59:29.830
And hopefully, we'll have a better chicken barrage.

01:59:30.000 --> 01:59:35.480
don't understand what's going on. Thank you for watching. Maybe we should have Jack Taylor throw

01:59:35.480 --> 01:59:47.340
chickens. I'll see ya. Thanks a lot. You've seen Juan. Never mind. Chucky from North Riverside

01:59:47.340 --> 01:59:52.050
loves to watch The People's Court. Weekdays at 1 and 4 on WCIU Channel 26.
